<h1>HR CRM Module-Wise API Documentation</h1>
<p>Generated from source code on 2026-04-02 16:04:17</p>
<p>This document explains the HR CRM API module by module. Each endpoint includes its purpose, access rules, request details, response details, and operational notes.</p>
<p class="sp"></p>
<h2>System Overview</h2>
<p><b>Technology stack:</b> ASP.NET Core Web API, .NET 8, Entity Framework Core, PostgreSQL, Swagger, JWT authentication, static files, and SignalR.</p>
<p><b>Default security model:</b> most endpoints require JWT authentication. Some endpoints also require explicit permissions or role-based checks.</p>
<p><b>Real-time endpoints:</b> /hubs/location and /hubs/notifications.</p>
<p class="sp"></p>
<h2>Attendance Module</h2>
<p><b>Module description:</b> Handles employee check-in, check-out, attendance history, total hours, and live location tracking.</p>
<p><b>Base route:</b> api/Attendence</p>
<p><b>Endpoints in this module:</b> 8</p>
<p class="sp"></p>
<h3>Endpoint: POST api/Attendence/checkin</h3>
<p><b>What it does:</b> Handles the endpoint route api/Attendence/checkin.</p>
<p><b>Access:</b> JWT authentication required; Self-user validation is enforced for user-specific data</p>
<p><b>Request:</b> dto from body as AttendanceCheckInDto</p>
<p><b>Request fields:</b> UserId (int), Latitude (double?), Longitude (double?)</p>
<p><b>Success response:</b> Returns JSON fields: Message</p>
<p><b>Error response:</b> 400 Bad Request: new { Message = error }</p>
<p><b>Error response:</b> 401 Unauthorized</p>
<p><b>Error response:</b> 403 Forbidden</p>
<p class="sp"></p>
<h3>Endpoint: POST api/Attendence/check-out</h3>
<p><b>What it does:</b> Handles the endpoint route api/Attendence/check-out.</p>
<p><b>Access:</b> JWT authentication required; Self-user validation is enforced for user-specific data</p>
<p><b>Request:</b> userId from route/query as int</p>
<p><b>Success response:</b> Returns JSON fields: Message, UserId, Time</p>
<p><b>Error response:</b> 400 Bad Request: &quot;No active check-in found&quot;</p>
<p><b>Error response:</b> 401 Unauthorized</p>
<p><b>Error response:</b> 403 Forbidden</p>
<p class="sp"></p>
<h3>Endpoint: GET api/Attendence/total-hours</h3>
<p><b>What it does:</b> Fetches data for api/Attendence/total-hours.</p>
<p><b>Access:</b> JWT authentication required; Additional role-based checks are applied in controller logic; Self-user validation is enforced for user-specific data</p>
<p><b>Request:</b> userId from route/query as int</p>
<p><b>Success response:</b> Returns JSON fields: UserId, TotalHoursHistory</p>
<p><b>Error response:</b> 404 Not Found: &quot;No attendance history found&quot;</p>
<p><b>Error response:</b> 401 Unauthorized</p>
<p><b>Error response:</b> 403 Forbidden</p>
<p class="sp"></p>
